irst\" isn't about grouping folders above files? It literally says \"Folder first\". Yes it is.\n\nHmm, but wait: with Folder first unchecked, the order is Zeta, Indent2, Indent, Money, Notes, Regex2, Regex, Shopping, Single, todo. That's exactly same as before. So toggling Folder first had no visible effect at all. Could be that the app is not persisting/applying it — or that grouping pass always runs. The changed note says \"directory grouping pass is now applied on every sort\" — that strongly suggests a regression where folders are always grouped first regardless of the option. So report: with \"Folder first\" unchecked, folder still appears before files.\n\nBut before reporting, let me verify the persisted state by reopening the dialog: Folder first should be unchecked. Then verify with a different sort (Date) to see folder still first. Also check \"Folder local\" maybe unchecked to see if it changes anything.\n\nActually, wait. Maybe \"Folder local\" is the one that should control it, and \"Folder first\" controls...? Both can't. Let me test: uncheck Folder first (already unchecked), also uncheck Folder local, apply, observe. If Zeta still first, then both ignored, reinforcing bug. Let me do that.\n\nActually careful: changing \"Folder local\" to off caused earlier weird state. Let me just do it and observe with screenshot."}
