e \"Folder local\" row might have moved). Let me not overthink.\n\nNow current state: Name ascending, folder NOT first (Zeta last). So the \"Folder first\" option works. My bug report was premature/wrong? The developer confirmed it though. Hmm — \"thanks, confirmed and logged\". That's concerning but the tool says confirmed. Maybe the bug IS real: the setting is not applied until re-entering the screen. Hmm.\n\nWait, let me re-examine. Maybe the list DID re-sort with Zeta last on OK, but I misread? The observe after OK clearly showed Zeta at [8] first. So it wasn't applied immediately. That's a bug in itself: sort changes not applied until revisit. But the developer confirmed my report as stated. Honestly the observed symptom \"Zeta still first with Folder first unchecked\" was true at the moment. But now, after navigation, it's fixed. That suggests the bug is a refresh issue rather than ignoring the option. Hmm.\n\nHold on. Let me reconsider the \"Folder local\" (floppy icon) meaning: per-folder sort saved locally. Maybe \"Folder local\" checked means \"apply sort only locally to this folder\" and when checked, the OK might not persist globally... but then after navigation, it did persist.\n\nLet me test again cleanly to determine the actual behavior and avoid false reporting:\n1. Current: Name sort, Zeta last (folder first off).\n2. Open sort dialog: check \"Folder first\" back on, OK. Observe immediately: does Zeta move to first?\n3. If not, leave screen and return: does it move?\n\nIf \"not applied until revisit\" → report symptom: sort changes require leaving/re-entering the file browser. That's a real bug.\n\nActually wait. There's a subtlety: The dialog \"Folder local\" option — perhaps when checked, the sort settings are stored per-folder, and the UI applies based on the stored value at creation. But the changed note about directory grouping suggests something else.\n\nLet me test now. Open sort, check Folder first, OK, observe immediate."}
