{"type": "thinking", "text": "todo view mode shows plain \"(A) Pay rent\" — fine.\n\nNow, view mode styling could have a bug only detectable via particular stylesheet features. Let me think about what \"stylesheet applied from assets rather than inline on each render\" could break visibly. In Markor, the view mode styling includes code highlighting (highlight.js?) or the markdown renderer's CSS. If loaded from assets, maybe the CSS path resolution differs: e.g., the CSS might fail to load for .md files not in the default folder, showing unstyled HTML. But our files are in the default folder.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the CSS loads asynchronously after content, and the first render lacks styling (flash), but that's not observable via static checks.\n\nHmm. Let me compare the expected Markor default styling with what we see. In Markor default theme, headings are dark, links are blue-ish? Our screenshot shows the link green (#2e7d32?). Hmm. Markor's default CSS uses \"a { color: #1a73e8 }\"? Not sure. The green might be from the highlighted markdown link color? Wait, in view mode the link is rendered by Markor's Markdown parser as `<a>`; the CSS `a` color in Markor's default stylesheet is likely #3f51b5 or similar. Green seems unusual but could be the actual default (#2e7d32?). Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the screenshot again. Tapping \"the guide\" link (green) may open the URL. Let me check Notes.md view mode once more and take a screenshot to examine. Also test that view mode reflects recent edits: edit content, save, view mode shows updated. That's a consistency check.\n\nActually, an important consistency test for view mode: after editing a file and switching to view mode, the rendered content should update (stylesheet applied from assets vs inline could relate to caching). Let me test: edit Shopping.md (add \"- bread\"), switch to view mode, check it shows bread; then undo.\n\nHmm, but more important: The changed note may hide a bug where the stylesheet is applied only on first render, so after editing text, view mode shows stale styling or stale content. Let me test.\n\nPlan:\n1. Open Shopping.md edit mode (we're in todo view mode now).\n2. In edit mode, append a bullet \"- bread\".\n3. Save (auto-save? Markor auto-saves on leave maybe; save button becomes enabled; tap save).\n4. Switch to View Mode → check content shows - bread.\n5. Back to edit, remove (undo), save.\n\nAlso test switching view/edit repeatedly (repetition).\n\nLet me navigate: from todo view mode, More → File Browser → Shopping.md.\n\nActually simpler: use the \"File Browser\" menu. Tap More (3)."}
