{"type": "thinking", "text": "The link \"the guide\" is green. Hmm. Is green the expected link color in Markor's default stylesheet? Let me think about Markor's default CSS. I recall Markor has themes and the default markdown stylesheet is based on \"github-markdown.css\"? Github markdown link color is #0366d6 (blue). Green (#2e7d32?) is Material green 800. Hmm, actually I recall that Markor's default stylesheet defines:\n\n```\na { color: #2e7d32; }\n```\n\nMaybe yes; Markor's app primary accent might be green in older versions? Markor's icon/brand color is reddish. Hmm.\n\nActually Markor's default CSS (assets/markor_default.css?) might be:\n```\nbody { ... }\na { color: #1565C0; }\n```\nI'm not sure. Without a reference, I can't call the green color a bug.\n\nBut maybe the view mode styling bug is that the link is underlined and green but heading underline is there — all styling present. So maybe view mode is fine.\n\nWait — maybe the issue is *the stylesheet is applied only to `md` files but not to `txt`* (plain text view mode has no styling needed). Hmm.\n\nLet me think about what a deliberately planted bug would look like given the change note. \"the stylesheet is now applied from the app's assets rather than inline on each render.\" Possible bug: The stylesheet is loaded from assets but the asset path is wrong (typo) so the CSS fails to load, resulting in default WebView styling. Default WebView styling would render links blue with underline (we see green), h1 bold larger without border-bottom (we see an underline). So CSS loads.\n\nAnother possibility: the stylesheet is applied to the *edit* mode's highlight colors? No.\n\nAnother: The stylesheet is applied to view mode but not to the \"preview\" of the first render after cold start; subsequent renders are fine. We can't cold start without clearing data? We could force-stop the app and reopen (open_app). The instruction says don't change data outside testing; force stop is fine. Let's test: force-stop (press HOME then open_app? open_app just brings to foreground, doesn't reset). Actually we can use press_key HOME then open_app to recreate? Not necessarily kills. Hmm. Not needed.\n\nMaybe the bug relates to the CSS being applied while *offline*? It's from assets, so fine.\n\nLet me test view mode for the same file in landscape (rotation) to see if styling persists."}
