ccent (red) but is green. Hmm, Markor's default CSS in newer versions uses:\n```\na { color: #4CAF50; }\n```\nHmm, not sure.\n\nLet me look for other clues: The editor's syntax highlighting shows \"# Shopping\" in orange, list markers in black, text in black, link URL in blue. That's the highlight theme.\n\nI think view mode styling is probably fine. But there must be something planted. The instructions mention 4 changes; typically 1-2 are buggy. We found 2 (sort grouping, duplicate line). Maybe view mode and search/replace are fine. But the task says sweep and sign off when no remaining bugs.\n\nHowever, one thing bugged me earlier: In view mode, tapping the ☰ in the selection toolbar switched to view mode. That was probably because the selection's floating toolbar \"☰\" is actually a \"View mode\" button? Wait: In Markor, when you select text and tap the \"☰\" (hamburger) in the floating toolbar, it might open the \"Text actions\" bottom sheet; but we saw the screen switch to View Mode. Let me investigate: was that a bug (tapping a selection action unexpectedly opens view mode)? Actually, maybe the ☰ item opened the \"View mode\" of the *selected text*? Hmm.\n\nLet me reproduce: Edit Single.md, select the word \"gamma\", tap the ☰ in the floating toolbar, and see what happens. If it switches to view mode, that could be a real bug (line actions \"☰\" does the wrong thing). But wait — maybe ☰ *is* \"Open in view mode\" for the selected link? Hmm.\n\nActually! I recall Markor's text selection floating toolbar: for selected text, there are actions like \"Open\" (if URL), \"Cut\", \"Copy\", \"Format\" (☰?), \"Share\". The ☰ icon likely opens the \"Format\" menu (bold/italic/etc.). It shouldn't switch to view mode. Our observation: tapping ☰ switched to view mode. Hmm, but maybe it opened a menu that we then dismissed with the subsequent tap? Let me re-read the timeline:\n\n1. Long-press in Notes editor → floating toolbar (Open, Cut, Copy, ☰, Share, ...).\n2. Tap element 7 (the ☰ TextView) → observe same toolbar, keyboard uppercase (maybe selection changed?).\n3. Tap element 7 again → same.\n4. Tap overflow (10) → Select all menu.\n5. Tap element 6 (☰ LinearLayout) → switched to view mode.\n\nSteps 2-3 tapped the ☰ *TextView* element (id floating_toolbar_menu_item_text), step 5 tapped the LinearLayout (its parent). Maybe the TextView is not clickable (though marked clickable?) and taps didn't register; step 5's tap on the LinearLayout registered and executed the action. The action switched to view mode? Hmm. Maybe the ☰ in the selection toolbar is \"View mode\" indeed? Hmm, Markor's selection toolbar has \"Open\", \"Cut\", \"Copy\", \"Text actions\" (☰?), \"Share\". The ☰ could open a secondary menu of \"text actions\" which includes \"View mode\"? Unlikely.\n\nWait, maybe the ☰ is \"More\" which opens a popup menu; and the popup contained an item that I then inadvertently tapped? No, step 5 was a single tap that immediately showed view mode in the observe.\n\nHmm, actually hold on: Maybe the tap at (615,267) landed on the app's *toolbar* view mode icon? In portrait, the toolbar is at y≈136, and the floating toolbar at y≈267. The tap target (615,267) is the ☰. Fine.\n\nBut note: after switching to view mode, the toolbar showed \"Edit Mode\". That is consistent with tapping the \"View Mode\" button. Where is the View Mode button? At (817,136). Not (615,267).\n\nUnless the coordinates in the floating toolbar observation were stale and the actual floating toolbar had moved/closed, so the tap at (615,267) hit the document content area, and the tap being on the link \"the guide\" maybe opened the URL? No, that would open a browser.\n\nHmm, wait: Maybe the tap landed on the *link* \"the guide\" and opened... no, we were in edit mode; the cursor was on the link; \"Open selected URL\" button was in the floating toolbar (element 0). If the floating toolbar had closed and the tap at (615,267) landed on the document, nothing would happen.\n\