bug and whether there is a second sort bug: the change note says \"File browser sort menu: the directory grouping pass is now applied on every sort.\" Perhaps the planted bug is that the grouping is applied twice or uses the wrong comparator such that in Reverse order, folders appear at the top instead of bottom? We tested reverse: folder remained first (with Folder first ON) — correct. With Folder first OFF... bug logged.\n\nMaybe test \"Size\" and \"MIME\" with folder first off to confirm grouping applied regardless — already did Date and Size. Fine.\n\nLet me now think about the \"editing actions\" area beyond line ops and search/replace: formatting actions (bold, heading, list, indent), undo/redo, save. The changed area is specifically line actions menu. We tested duplicate, indent, delete (via controls). Maybe test line action with multiple lines selected: \"Duplicate lines\" should duplicate all selected lines. That's a good boundary test. Use Indent2.md ('- a' then '  - deep'), select both lines? Selecting all is hard via long-press + drag. Could use \"Select all\" from the overflow then tap Duplicate lines. Selecting all lines then Duplicate should duplicate the entire text. Let's test on Single.md? Selecting all \"gamma\" then duplicate should give \"gamma\\ngamma\" maybe (no trailing newline → bug?). Hmm, might behave differently. It could reveal the same bug.\n\nActually, maybe the \"no trailing newline\" bug is what the task intends: \"Editor line actions menu: the line-cloning action now computes its insertion point after the line break.\" Single.md's no-newline precondition is definitely a hint. We tested and found it does nothing. Hmm, wait: is \"does nothing\" the actual intended correct behavior? Maybe the expected behavior for a last-line clone is to insert a newline + line, but with the \"fix\" it computes after the line break; if there's no line break at EOF, maybe it should append \"\\n\"+line. Doing nothing seems wrong either way.\n\nBut hold on — maybe the real bug is different: for a line WITH a trailing newline, the clone might be inserted after the *next* line break (i.e., one line too far), not immediately after. In Indent.md, duplicating line 2 (last content line, followed by \\n) produced a duplicate right after line 2 — correct. Hmm.\n\nWhat about duplicating line 1 of a multi-line file? We tried to place cursor on line 1 but apparently hit line 2. Let me test with a file where line 1 is clearly distinguishable and ensure cursor on line 1. I can tap at the very top-left of the text. For Indent.md, line 1 \"- item\" at y≈? In the screenshot of Shopping, \"# Shopping\" was at y≈290 in portrait, and \"- milk\" at y≈380. The line height ~50. Tapping at y=300 would be line 1. Earlier I tapped (120,295) in landscape for Indent.md and it duplicated line 2, suggesting line 1 was at y≈250-280 and line 2 at 280-310. Hmm.\n\nTo be certain, I could use the cursor position via keyboard: after tapping, press HOME? That moves cursor to line start. Not needed.\n\nAlternative approach: create a fresh test by typing content into an empty file (new file) with clear:false — but creating a new file changes data (allowed for testing but I'd delete it). Hmm, Creating a file named e.g. \"QATest.md\" then deleting is acceptable? \"Do not change data outside what testing requires.\" Creating a temp test file is within testing. That would let me control content exactly and test line actions on line 1, middle, last-with-newline, last-without-newline. But I already have a confirmed bug for no-trailing-newline. Additional details not needed.\n\nLet me instead test \"Duplicate lines\" on the *first* line of a controlled file to see if insertion point is correct. I can use Notes.md: select all? Hmm.\n\nActually, let me directly test with the cursor visually using the screenshot: In Notes.md edit mode, place cursor at end of line 1 \"# Notes\" then tap Duplicate. If it duplicates line 1 correctly, then insertion after line break works for line 1 (with newline). We already saw line 2 of Indent works. So both fine.\n\nI think the line action area is covered: bug found for no-trailing-newline.\n\nNow, let me double-check the duplicate bug is not caused by the line action requiring a selection: in Single.md, \"Duplicate lines\" did nothing, but \"Delete lines\" removed the entire text and \"Indent\" indented. So the action itself is a no-op for no-newline. Confirmed.\n\nCould there be another bug in the line actions: \"Delete lines\" removed the whole content including the trailing newline, which is expected for deleting the only line. Fine.\n\nLet me close the selection toolbar by pressing BACK (to dismiss) and then verify no data changes in Notes.md.\n\nLet me press BACK once (dismiss selection toolbar) — careful: back might exit editor. Since the floating toolbar is showing, back should deselect. Then check content."}
