{"type": "thinking", "text": "Saved (Save disabled). Notes.md is back to its original content. \n\nNow let me consider whether the changed file browser sort grouping has additional subtle bug: When \"Reverse order\" is ON with \"Folder first\" ON, folder stays first — tested. When \"Folder first\" OFF + Reverse ON, Zeta should be... at the end? Actually reverse name with no grouping: Zeta first (Z is last alphabetically → first in reverse). So with folder first OFF and reverse, Zeta first is correct. Fine.\n\nLet me now do a final sanity check of the sort bug with \"Folder first\" OFF and Name sort after a *fresh* list refresh, to see whether the folder position is last or first. It seems non-deterministic. But the confirmed report covers it.\n\nHmm, one more thought: the precondition says a folder Zeta. The sort changed note says \"directory grouping pass is now applied on every sort\". Maybe the intended bug is that the folder grouping is applied *even when sorting by Date/Size/MIME*, where folder names shouldn't matter... no, \"Folder first\" is independent.\n\nWait, maybe \"Folder local\" is not \"save per folder\" but rather \"Directory grouping local\"? Ugh.\n\nActually, let me reconsider \"Folder local\" meaning: In Markor, there is a preference \"Sort by folder local\"?? Hmm, in Markor's Settings there's \"Filesystem: Sort\" with option \"Folder local\" meaning \"sort folder names by their own locale\"? Unlikely.\n\nLet me look at the Markor source strings I might recall: \n```\n<string name=\"sort_by\">Sort by</string>\n<string name=\"sort_by_name\">Name</string>\n<string name=\"sort_by_date\">Date</string>\n<string name=\"sort_by_size\">Size</string>\n<string name=\"sort_by_mime_type\">MIME type</string>\n<string name=\"sort_by_folder_first\">Folder first</string>\n<string name=\"sort_by_reverse\">Reverse order</string>\n<string name=\"sort_by_folder_local\">Folder local</string>\n<string name=\"sort_by_dotfiles\">.dotfiles</string>\n```\nHmm, \"Folder local\" might mean \"Sort order is local per folder\" indeed. In Markor, there is a setting \"sort_by_folder_local\" maybe described as \"Remember sort per folder\". The floppy icon supports that.\n\nOK. The bug remains: \"Folder first\" off yet folder first. Developer confirmed. Good.\n\nNow, we should consider whether to file the \"sort not applied until re-enter\" as a separate bug. The developer already confirmed the first report; it's logged. I'll not duplicate.\n\nLet me look at one more potential issue in the file browser area: the file list \"..\" row description shows the parent path, and the first row description says \"/storage/emulated/0/Documents\" while in Zeta it shows \"/storage/emulated/0/Documents/markor\" — wait, that was odd earlier. Let me re-examine: At root (notebook folder), the \"..\" row shows \"/storage/emulated/0/Documents\". Inside Zeta, \"..\" shows \"/storage/emulated/0/Documents/markor\". If Zeta is at Documents/Zeta, its parent is Documents, not Documents/markor. Hmm! Wait, unless the notebook folder is /storage/emulated/0/Documents/markor and the root \"..\" shows the parent /storage/emulated/0/Documents. But then Zeta would be at .../markor/Zeta, and inside Zeta the parent would be .../markor — which matches \"/storage/emulated/0/Documents/markor\"! So the root listing is of the markor folder (notebook), displayed path parent as Documents. But then the header \"Markor\" and root row \"Folder Documents /storage/emulated/0/Documents\" is the \"..\" (parent). Yes consistent. Fine.\n\nWait, but the precondition says \"The notebook folder contains ... and a folder Zeta.\" And the app's notebook folder may be /storage/emulated/0/Documents (in this test build) or /Documents/markor. Doesn't matter.\n\nNow let me test the \"Go to\" quick access? Not in scope.\n\nLet me reconsider the editing actions area for a bug: the change note \"Editor line actions menu: the line-cloning action now computes its insertion point after the line break.\" There might be a bug with duplicating a line that ends with a newline producing the clone *before* the line break (merging). We tested Indent line 2 and it duplicated correctly (content \"- item\\n  - child\\n  - child\\n\"). So works when newline exists. And no-op when no newline. Good.\n\nMaybe also test duplicating a selected multi-line block: Select all (via long-press overflow → Select all) then Duplicate lines; expected whole text duplicated once (with a newline between). On a file with trailing newline, e.g., Indent2.md \"- a\\n  - deep\\n\": Select all → duplicate → \"- a\\n  - deep\\n- a\\n  - deep\\n\"? Let's test on a file and undo. This is \"repetition/inputs\" but maybe overkill. Yet a bug could exist in multi-line cloning insertion point. Let me test quickly on Indent2.md.\n\nActually, the changed code might be about \"insertion point after the line break\" for selected lines too. Testing multi-line selection could reveal a bug: e.g., duplicate might insert at the wrong place and reorder lines. Let me test.\n\nSteps:\n1. Open Indent2.md (from browser).\n2. Long-press a word, tap overflow → Select all (selects all).\n3. Tap \"Duplicate lines\" (need landscape for that icon? In portrait, line action icons are not all visible; but the selection toolbar covers; we need the format bar's Duplicate lines. In portrait the format bar shows up to Heading1. Duplicate lines is not visible. Could rotate landscape after selecting? Rotating may lose selection. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: Use the editor's \"Select all\" from the format bar? The overflow in selection toolbar has Select all. After selecting all, tap the editor toolbar \"Duplicate lines\" in landscape. Selection might survive rotation? Not guaranteed.\n\nAlternatively, use Indent2.md in landscape from the start: open, rotate, long-press to select word, then Select all via overflow, then tap Duplicate lines. Let me try.\n\nDo I really need this? The task says test thoroughly. I've got time/steps. Let's do it.\n\nFirst, current state: Notes.md edit mode. Navigate to Indent2.md: More options (6) → File Browser → Indent2.md (11). Then rotate landscape, select all, duplicate.\n\nLet me do it."}
