{"type": "thinking", "text": "Indent worked on the selection: content \"    - a\\n      - deep\\n    \" (note selection included trailing newline; it indented the trailing empty line too). So taps register. Therefore \"Duplicate lines\" with all-text selected did nothing. That's another manifestation: duplication no-op when selection extends to EOF? Hmm, or maybe when selection includes the whole text.\n\nWait, maybe I tapped Duplicate while the selection was *all* (including trailing newline). Duplicating all lines should double the text. It did nothing. This might be the same root bug: insertion point after the line break — if the selection's end is at the last line break (EOF), there's no \"next\" line break? Hmm.\n\nInteresting. So \"Duplicate lines\" fails in two cases: (1) single-line no newline; (2) entire text selected (ending with newline). Hmm, maybe the general failure is when the selection/line ends at the document end. Perhaps the bug is that cloning only works when there's text *after* the line break (i.e., a following line exists). In Indent.md earlier, duplicating line 2 (last content line, last line break at EOF, no text after) DID work. Hmm, contradiction.\n\nWait, let me re-check that earlier Indent.md duplication: content was \"- item\\n  - child\\n\" and after duplicate became \"- item\\n  - child\\n  - child\\n\". That is duplicating the last line (which ends with \\n at EOF) worked. So the \"selection\" case is different.\n\nHmm, maybe Duplicate lines with a selection duplicates the *selected* line including selection, and the insertion is at the selection end; if selection is all text, the insertion at the end? Should still duplicate.\n\nMaybe the issue: \"Select all\" selection is the whole text, and the line-based action operates on lines intersecting the selection; with all text selected including the trailing newline, the \"current line\" logic might be an empty line after EOF, so duplication of an empty last line → nothing? But then for Indent.md the cursor was on line 2 (content), worked.\n\nHmm, this could be a genuine additional bug: \"Duplicate lines\" does nothing when the whole document is selected. But is that within the reported symptom? The developer already confirmed the no-trailing-newline case. I could file another report for the selection-all case. But maybe they're the same underlying code (insertion point after the line break — when selection ends at document end, insertion point at EOF, and the code inserts nothing?).\n\nHold on, actually let me reconsider: maybe when all text is selected, tapping \"Duplicate lines\" DID do something, but the *undo* state? Observe after tap shows content unchanged and undo disabled. So no.\n\nHmm wait, actually after the Select all, I tapped element 31 \"Duplicate lines\" — but is element 31 the right icon? In the post-select-all observation, element 31 is \"ImageView desc=Duplicate lines\" @(1667,438). Yes.\n\nHmm, but note that after the selection, the floating toolbar covers y=412 from x≈920-1335 (Cut/Copy/☰/Share) — the Duplicate icon at x=1667 is clear. So the tap should hit. And Indent at x=1782 worked. So Duplicate no-op confirmed.\n\nShould I report this separately? The instruction: \"Reproduce a problem once before you report it.\" We have one instance. Let me reproduce once more to be safe: currently content is indented with selection probably lost (after Indent, selection may be gone? Observe shows no floating toolbar — selection cleared). Let me undo the indent first, then redo the select-all + duplicate test.\n\nUndo (element 1)."}
