{"type": "thinking", "text": "Restored \"- a\\n  - deep\\n\".\n\nNow, about the select-all duplicate no-op: it could be considered a bug. But is it in scope and is it clearly wrong? In Markor, the \"Duplicate lines\" action should duplicate selected lines. When all lines are selected, it should duplicate them. Doing nothing is likely wrong. But is this the planted bug or just how Markor behaves (maybe it requires cursor and ignores selection)? If it ignores selection, then with all text selected, the cursor line might be the last (empty) line after the trailing newline → duplicating an empty line → inserting a newline? Observed no change. Hmm.\n\nActually! Important: after selecting all, the cursor/anchor is at the end. The \"current line\" might be the empty line after the final newline (line 3). Duplicating an empty line at EOF would insert... nothing? Actually duplicating an empty last line would add a newline, which would be visible as an extra blank line. Observed content unchanged, so no insertion. This is consistent with the same no-trailing-line-break logic? Hmm: line 3 is empty with no line break after it, so cloning it does nothing (same bug pattern). So likely one root cause: cloning a line that has no line break after it (EOF) does nothing. That's exactly the Single.md case. And when all text is selected, the \"current line\" ends up being the empty line after the final newline (which has no line break after) → no-op. So the two observations share the same root cause, which I've already reported. Good — no need for a second report.\n\nSo the line-cloning bug: it only works for lines followed by a line break and not the cursor's line? Well, Indent.md line 2 with trailing \\n worked. So the rule: it fails on the final line without a trailing newline (whether content line or empty line). That's the Single.md case. Report stands.\n\nNow clean up: Indent2.md is at original content; save is disabled (undo disabled) → saved? Wait, we undid the change; Save butt