{"type": "thinking", "text": "Restored: Folder first ON, folder Zeta first.\n\nNotes.md timestamp updated 12:42 due to test edit and revert. Content is back to original. Fine.\n\nBefore signing off, let me reconsider whether there are other bugs in the three areas. Let me think about the view mode \"stylesheet from assets\" bug possibility again. The key visible artifact of \"stylesheet applied from assets\" could be the **syntax highlighting in view mode of code blocks**? Not testable.\n\nWait, maybe there's a bug with the view mode *scrolling* after rotating? No.\n\nWhat about \"view mode\" opening logic: .md files sometimes open in view mode, sometimes edit mode. We saw Notes.md open in view mode the first time, then edit mode later; Shopping opened view then edit; Single opened edit; Regex2 opened edit; todo edit. The behavior likely depends on the app setting \"Open .md in view mode\" or the last used mode per file. Hmm, could there be a bug where view mode isn't remembered? Not necessarily.\n\nActually, maybe the \"view mode\" area includes the \"open as view\" button in the file browser's long-press context menu. Let me check long-press on a file in the browser: it may show \"Open with\", \"View\", \"Edit\", \"Rename\", etc. Hmm, in Markor, long-pressing a file shows a context menu with \"Open with\", \"Rename\", \"Delete\", \"Copy\", \"Move\", \"Info\", maybe \"Set as homepage\". Not sure.\n\nI think we should also test the file browser's Search action (the magnifier in the file browser). That's part of \"file browser\" area? It's a search across files. Actually, the \"Search\" button in the file browser toolbar might be \"Search in files\" (full-text search) — worth checking since a precondition file with content is set. Hmm, but the areas are \"file browser and its sort options\" (so sort focus), \"editing actions and search/replace\" (editor search), \"view mode\".\n\nMaybe the file-browser Search is the same \"search/replace\" feature? No, the toolbar search in the file browser opens a file search (recently modified?). Let me peek: tap the file browser Search (element 3). This is a navigation route test too. Let me check what it does.\n\nActually, the file browser toolbar has: Go to (folder icon), Sort by, Search, More options. The Search likely opens a search dialog to find files by name. Not in the listed areas exactly. But \"Navigation: reach screens by more than one route\" etc. I could skip.\n\nI've spent many steps. Let me do a final check of a few state/reversal behaviors in view mode:\n- View mode → rotate → back: content intact (done).\n- View mode → edit → view: content intact (done).\n- View mode for Shopping/Indent/Single/Money/Regex/todo (done).\n\nI think the sweep is complete with 2 confirmed bugs. But hold on — the task says the changed items include \"Search and replace dialog: the replace field is now built below the search field.\" Why would this be a bug? Perhaps the bug is that the replace field appears ABOVE the search field in some state, or the replace field is missing when re-opened. We tested portrait/landscape: below. Also toggling off/on works. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the bug is that the *Replace* field is rendered below the search field but the \"Preserve Case\" and \"Replace\" buttons are misaligned? Looking at the portrait observation: replace row buttons at y=503: Clear @705, Preserve Case @810, Replace (1) @915, Replace all @1020. The search row: Clear @600, New Line @705, Match Case @810, Whole Word @915, Regex @1020. In the replace row, the \"Clear\" is at x=705 (aligned with search's New Line), leaving a gap at 600. That's fine.\n\nHmm, what about the \"replace field built below the search field\" — maybe in some builds the replace field was above; now below. Seems correct.\n\nMaybe there's a bug where *the replace field's hint text is \"Search\"* instead of \"Replace\"? Observed \"Replace\". Fine.\n\nCould there be a bug where the replace field is *editable but the replacement uses the search text*? We verified correct replacement.\n\nOK.\n\nNow, before signing off, let me reconsider the first bug report's wording once more: I said \"folder grouping applied on every sort regardless of Folder first.\" Clean repro confirms. Good.\n\nAnd the second: duplicate lines no-op on no-trailing-newline. Confirmed.\n\nAre there any other obvious bugs I noticed but dismissed?\n- Sort setting changes appear not to refresh immediately (but sometimes do). This is related to the same folder-first bug? Actually we saw: after unchecking Folder first, the list still showed Zeta first immediately; later, after navigation, once Zeta was last, then later it was first again. The inconsistency is the same bug: grouping pass applied on every sort. Since the grouping pass now runs on every sort, the folder-first pref is ignored on sort operations but honored on initial load (folder last). That explains everything: initial load after leaving/re-entering uses saved order (Zeta last); any subsequent sort via the dialog or adapter re-sort applies grouping (Zeta first). And when I observed Zeta first after re-entering, that entry's load probably triggered a sort (or the saved order was already grouped?). Hmm, fine.\n\n- Search clear leaves stale counter: minor, not reported.\n\n- The selection toolbar ☰ toggling keyboard shift: not understood, not reported.\n\n- Rotation closes search bars: common behavior, not reported.\n\n- Notes.md \"open mode\" varies: probably intended (remembers last mode). Not a bug.\n\nHmm, wait. There's one thing I should double check: the view mode \"Search\" button in the toolbar (ImageView desc=\"Search\", id=search_button) in view mode opens a search that found \"1/1\". Is that part of \"editing actions and search/replace\" or \"view mode\"? It works.\n\nWhat about view mode of a file long enough to need scrolling? None are long.\n\nLet me also test that \"View Mode\" is reachable from the file browser by more than one route: e.g., long-press file → \"Open with\"? Hmm. On second thought, maybe the app supports opening a file in *view mode* via a long-press menu option (\"View\"/\"Edit\"), which would be the \"more than one route\". Let me check the file context menu quickly: long-press a file row in the browser. This could reveal a \"View\" option. If it exists, test it works and shows styled content. Let me try long-press Notes.md row (element 20).\n\nActually careful: long-press might start drag-and-drop or show context menu. Let's try."}
