{"type": "thinking", "text": "Back in browser with initial-ish state (Folder first ON; Zeta first).\n\nI want to conduct one last check on view mode styling: maybe the bug is that view mode does NOT apply the stylesheet to **plain text (.txt)**? Not relevant.\n\nLet me think about whether \"stylesheet applied from assets\" could cause the *view mode to show unstyled content after first entering a file from a cold state*. To simulate cold start, I could force-stop the app via settings? The tools don't have force-stop, but pressing HOME and using open_app won't kill it. We could open another app then come back; not a cold start. Skip.\n\nAlternatively, the \"Reload\" menu item in the file browser might reload the current file; not styling.\n\nHmm, maybe I should test view mode of `Notes.md` *after* the app process was in the background for a while / after rotation. Done.\n\nAt this point, I've tested all three areas thoroughly:\n1. File browser & sort: all sort types, reverse, folder first on/off, folder local, dotfiles (not toggled — hmm, .dotfiles not tested! The folder has no dotfiles, so toggling would show nothing. Skip).\n2. Editing actions: duplicate (bug), indent, de-indent, delete, bold, select all, undo/redo, save/persist; search/replace: basic, regex, groups, replace all, toggles, empty, orientation.\n3. View mode: Notes (heading/link), Indent (nested list), Shopping (heading/list), Money, Regex, Regex2, todo, inside; view/edit toggling, rotation, search in view mode, content consistency after edits.\n\nTwo bugs confirmed. Are there any remaining? Let me reconsider the \"Copy\" vs \"Cut\" etc. Not needed.\n\nWait — one more thought about the changed \"search and replace dialog: replace field below the search field\". What if in *landscape*, the replace field overlaps the editor or is cut off? We saw positions: search at y=356, replace at y=482, editor top y=?? fine.\n\nWhat about *font scale*? no.\n\nLet me also double check the \"replace all\" button when there are no matches / empty replace: With empty replace field and a search match, tapping Replace should delete the match. That's expected. Quick test? We did replace with text. Not needed.\n\nOne more: what if replace field is empty and you tap Replace (1)? It deletes the match — expected. Not a bug.\n\nWhat about regex invalid pattern causing crash? E.g., search \"[\" with regex on. Markor should show \"Invalid regex\" or \"No results\", not crash. That's an \"input: unusual values\" test for search. Let's test quickly on Notes.md: open search, enable regex, type \"[\" and press search. If the app crashes, that's a bug. Worth checking.\n\nLet me do it: open Notes.md (element 20), then search, toggle regex, type \"[\" press Search, observe."}
